<BaseLayout
 title="Branded Apparel Guides | Bighorn Threads"
 description="Read planning guides for branded apparel, decoration, company stores, and protective workwear. Confirm all PPE decisions with your employer and manufacturer."
 canonical="https://bighornthreads.com/blog/"
>
 <!-- Hero -->
 <section class="bg-concrete">
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pt-16 pb-16 sm:px-6 sm:pt-20 lg:px-8">
 <p class="kicker mb-3">Field Notes</p>
 <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-4xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-[0.95] tracking-tight text-charcoal sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
 Insights for <span class="text-gold-600">Construction &amp; Trades</span>
 </h1>
 <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash sm:text-xl">
 Educational guides on branded apparel, decoration methods, and company-store planning for people running crews in Las Vegas.
 </p>
 </div>
 </section>

 <!-- Editorial intro -->
 <section class="border-y border-hairline bg-paper py-16 sm:py-20">
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
 <p class="mb-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash">
 Field Notes is an educational archive for apparel planning. It covers decoration choices, bulk and store workflows, and questions to take to an employer safety lead before selecting protective apparel.
 </p>
 <p class="mb-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash">
 We write for general contractors, electrical shops, plumbing and HVAC companies, roofing crews, landscapers, and ironworkers. Bighorn provides Las Vegas account management and coordinates approved products and decoration through production partners.
 </p>
 <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash">
 Every post is written to be useful on its own. No fluff, no pivot-to-upsell, no "definitive guide" nonsense. If a section doesn't teach you something usable in the next quote you send or the next PPE decision you make, it doesn't go live.
 </p>
 </div>
 </section>

 <!-- Posts grid -->
 <section class="bg-concrete py-20">
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
 <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
 {posts.map((post) => (
 <a
 href={postPath(post.slug)}
 class="group relative flex flex-col border border-hairline bg-panel p-6 transition-colors hover:border-gold-500 sm:p-7"
 >
 <span
 aria-hidden="true"
 class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-0.5"
 style={`background:${accentFor(post.category)}`}
 ></span>
 <div class="mb-5 flex items-center gap-2">
 <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5" style={`background:${accentFor(post.category)}`}></span>
 <span class="spec text-gold-700">
 {post.category}
 </span>
 </div>
 <h2 class="mb-3 font-heading text-xl font-bold uppercase leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-charcoal transition-colors group-hover:text-gold-600">
 {post.title}
 </h2>
 <p class="mb-6 line-clamp-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ash">
 {post.excerpt}
 </p>
 <div class="mt-auto flex items-center justify-between border-t border-hairline pt-4">
 <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ash">
 {post.readTime} &middot; {post.date}
 </span>
 <span class="text-sm font-bold text-gold-600 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">
 Read &rarr;
 </span>
 </div>
 </a>
 ))}
 </div>

 <!-- Cadence footer -->
 <div class="mt-16 border-t border-hairline pt-10 text-center">
 <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ash">New planning guides added as available</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(blogSchema)} />
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemListSchema)} />

 <!-- CTA band -->
 <section class="border-t border-hairline bg-paper py-16">
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 text-center sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
 <p class="kicker mb-3 justify-center">Get Started</p>
 <h2 class="mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight text-charcoal sm:text-4xl">
 Ready to outfit your crew?
 </h2>
 <p class="mb-8 text-lg text-ash">
 Talk to a real human who has been outfitting Vegas trades today.
 </p>
 <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary text-base">
 Request a Quote
 </a>
 </div>
 </section>
</BaseLayout>
